      "@id": "editorial/skills/editorial-audits/voice-authoring-guidance.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Read the voices before the first sentence, not after the first review",
      "prov:value": "The active set is in the instance's config, its `index.config.json` entry\n(inline; a legacy `<name>.config.json` only until `index-config:migrate --inline`):\n\n```json\n{ \"voices\": { \"active\": [\"milnor\"] } }\n```"
    },
    {
      "@id": "editorial/skills/editorial-audits/voice-authoring-guidance.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Read the voices before the first sentence, not after the first review",
      "prov:value": "This\ninstance activates none: folio-assistant's own documentation carries no voice\n(issue #208).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#208"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "editorial/skills/editorial-audits/voice-authoring-guidance.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "The rules most often broken by drafting on instinct",
      "prov:value": "Two further examples stood here, both drawn from another instance's voices, and\nthey are gone because this is the PLATFORM. A voice's rules belong to the\ninstance that derived them, where each one carries the publication, page and\nverbatim quote it was read from. Restating a rule here reproduced it **without\nits citation**, in a subsystem whose whole argument is that a voice is auditable\nrather than asserted — and `check-voices.ts` exists because PR #210 shipped ten\nplausible rules with `source: null`, one of which asserted the opposite of what\nits own source says. The uncited copy is the one a reader meets first, and it is\nthe one nothing can check.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#210"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
